  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Calculate the minor of the entry ${b}_{22}$ in the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 13 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "The minor of ${b}_{22}=7$ (second row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $7$ are removed: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \u2217 & -6 \\\\ \u2217 & 7 & \u2217 \\\\ 5 & \u2217 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{22}=7$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 4-(-6)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =12-(-30) \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
